Installed-Size: 168899
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.38), libcap2 (>= 1:2.10), libgcc-s1 (>= 3.3.1), liblzma5 (>= 5.1.1alpha+20120614), libseccomp2 (>= 0.0.0~20120605), libstdc++6 (>= 13.1), zlib1g (>= 1:1.1.4)
Recommends: jq, curl, wget
Suggests: graphviz, python3-matplotlib
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/J-mazz/sys-scan-graph
Description: Advanced Linux Security Scanner Core
 Sys-Scan-Graph is a comprehensive Linux security and hygiene scanner that combines
 a high-performance C++20 core scanner with AI model files for intelligent analysis.
 .
 The core scanner performs fast host inspection across multiple security domains:
 processes, network sockets, kernel parameters, kernel modules, world-writable
 paths, SUID/SGID binaries, IOC heuristics, and MAC (SELinux/AppArmor) status.
 .
 This package provides the core C++ binary and pre-trained AI models.
 The Python Intelligence Layer is available separately as sys-scan-graph
 on PyPI, which provides AI-powered threat analysis and graph-based correlation.
